---
export const title = 'Portals';
export const order = 400;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A portal for customers signs some people in and shows others as visitors. Put a
  <code>wc-user-menu</code> in the <code>end</code> slot for someone signed in, and a Sign in link
  for a visitor; both stay in the bar at every width. The header takes its colours from the theme,
  so a portal's own primary colour and shape apply without extra styling.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; min-height: 240px; display: grid; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-site-header label='Pages' collapse-at='520'>
      <a slot='brand' href='#'>Acme Support</a>
      <wc-site-nav-link href='#'>Home</wc-site-nav-link>
      <wc-site-nav-menu label='Knowledge'>
        <wc-site-nav-link href='#'>Accounts</wc-site-nav-link>
        <wc-site-nav-link href='#'>Billing</wc-site-nav-link>
        <wc-site-nav-link href='#'>Troubleshooting</wc-site-nav-link>
      </wc-site-nav-menu>
      <wc-site-nav-link href='#' current>My tickets</wc-site-nav-link>
      <wc-user-menu slot='end' name='Ada Lovelace' email='ada@acme.example'></wc-user-menu>
    </wc-site-header>
    <wc-site-header label='Pages' collapse-at='520'>
      <a slot='brand' href='#'>Acme Support</a>
      <wc-site-nav-link href='#' current>Home</wc-site-nav-link>
      <wc-site-nav-link href='#'>Status</wc-site-nav-link>
      <wc-link-button slot='end' variant='text' href='#'>Sign in</wc-link-button>
    </wc-site-header>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Sticky headers</h3>
<p>
  <code>sticky</code> keeps the header at the top of the viewport as the page scrolls. Add
  <code>hide-on-scroll</code> to slide it away while the person scrolls down and back as soon as
  they scroll up. It never slides away while it holds focus or an open panel, and moves without
  animation when reduced motion is asked for.
</p>
